# Graph Builder Role

You receive a list of source files from a single module (directory) and their
contents. Respond with exactly two tagged lines — no prose, no preamble, nothing else.

## Output format

```
GRAPH_SUMMARY:<one paragraph — what this module does and why it exists>
GRAPH_SUBSYSTEM:<single word grouping — e.g. auth, billing, api, storage, graph, wiki, cli>
```

Rules:
- GRAPH_SUMMARY: one paragraph, no bullets, plain prose
- GRAPH_SUBSYSTEM: one word only
- Output exactly these two lines. Nothing else.


Module path: services/migrator-files/internal/reconcile
Files:

--- services/migrator-files/internal/reconcile/reconcile.go (824 lines) ---
// Package reconcile compares legacy and new-platform state after the
// 9 apply phases have run. For each phase it produces a PhaseReport
// containing:
//
//   - LegacyCount    — rows observed by the legacy reader
//   - SidecarCount   — entries in the phase's <RUN_DIR>/<phase>_map.json
//                       sidecar (= rows the migrator actually wrote)
//   - NewCount       — same as SidecarCount today; reserved for the
//                       day a server-side List/Count RPC lands
//   - CountParityOK  — LegacyCount == NewCount
//   - SampleSize / SampleMismatches / SampleErrors — deep-spot-check
//                       outcome (when the phase supports per-id Get)
//   - Notes          — first 5 mismatches' brief description + any
//                       phase-level caveats (legacy gaps, etc.)
//
// Strategy:
//
//	The migrator does not currently expose org-scoped List/Count RPCs
//	for entities, edges, chunks, or embeddings. Rather than add new
//	RPCs in this task we treat the sidecar count as the new-platform
//	count — that proves parity from the migrator's perspective and is
//	exactly what an operator wants to see for a cutover go/no-go.
//	When a future PR adds proper enumeration RPCs the NewCount field
//	will diverge from SidecarCount and the parity check will become
//	server-truth-based.
//
//	For deep-spot-check we use the per-id Get RPCs (every service
//	exposes them) to dereference a random sample of legacy_ids from
//	the sidecar and field-by-field compare against the legacy source.
//	Phases without a usable per-id read (embeddings, provenance) skip
//	the deep-spot-check and emit a clear note.
//
// Driver-level outcome (ReconcileReport.Mismatches) sums sample
// mismatches across every phase plus any phase that failed the count
// parity check; the CLI exits 2 if Mismatches > 0 so operators get a
// programmatic go/no-go signal.
package reconcile

import (
	"context"
	"errors"
	"fmt"
	"math/rand/v2"
	"sort"
	"time"

	"google.golang.org/grpc"

	corpusv1 "github.com/zenithflowinc/omnicore-platform/platform/proto/gen/go/omnicore/files/corpus/v1"
	documentv1 "github.com/zenithflowinc/omnicore-platform/platform/proto/gen/go/omnicore/files/document/v1"
	edgev1 "github.com/zenithflowinc/omnicore-platform/platform/proto/gen/go/omnicore/files/edge/v1"
	entityv1 "github.com/zenithflowinc/omnicore-platform/platform/proto/gen/go/omnicore/files/entity/v1"
	entitytypev1 "github.com/zenithflowinc/omnicore-platform/platform/proto/gen/go/omnicore/files/entity_type/v1"
	relationshiptypev1 "github.com/zenithflowinc/omnicore-platform/platform/proto/gen/go/omnicore/files/relationship_type/v1"

	"github.com/zenithflowinc/omnicore-platform/services/migrator-files/internal/legacy"
)

// Default sample size for the deep-spot-check. 100 was chosen for a
// reasonable confidence-without-burning-budget tradeoff per the
// reconcile design discussion. Operators can override via
// ReconcileInput.SampleSize.
const DefaultSampleSize = 100

// maxNotePerSampledMismatch caps the number of per-row mismatch notes
// captured in PhaseReport.Notes — the diagnostic signal saturates
// quickly and operators don't want a 5MB JSON file.
const maxNotePerSampledMismatch = 5

// EntityTypeGetClient is the gRPC subset reconcile needs for Phase 1
// deep-spot-check. Tests inject a fake; production wires the real
// EntityTypeServiceClient (which already implements this method).
type EntityTypeGetClient interface {
	Get(ctx context.Context, in *entitytypev1.GetRequest, opts ...grpc.CallOption) (*entitytypev1.GetResponse, error)
}

// RelationshipTypeGetClient is the gRPC subset reconcile needs for Phase
// 2 deep-spot-check.
type RelationshipTypeGetClient interface {
	Get(ctx context.Context, in *relationshiptypev1.GetRequest, opts ...grpc.CallOption) (*relationshiptypev1.GetResponse, error)
}

// CorpusGetClient is the gRPC subset reconcile needs for Phase 3
// deep-spot-check.
type CorpusGetClient interface {
	Get(ctx context.Context, in *corpusv1.GetRequest, opts ...grpc.CallOption) (*corpusv1.GetResponse, error)
}

// DocumentGetClient is the gRPC subset reconcile needs for Phase 4
// (and Phase 5 chunk parity, which uses the same connection).
type DocumentGetClient interface {
	Get(ctx context.Context, in *documentv1.GetRequest, opts ...grpc.CallOption) (*documentv1.GetResponse, error)
}

// EntityGetClient is the gRPC subset reconcile needs for Phase 7
// deep-spot-check.
type EntityGetClient interface {
	Get(ctx context.Context, in *entityv1.GetRequest, opts ...grpc.CallOption) (*entityv1.GetResponse, error)
}

// EdgeGetClient is the gRPC subset reconcile needs for Phase 8
// deep-spot-check.
type EdgeGetClient interface {
	Get(ctx context.Context, in *edgev1.GetRequest, opts ...grpc.CallOption) (*edgev1.GetResponse, error)
}

// LegacyChunkLister is the legacy-side reader used by the chunks +
// embeddings phases. The interface is satisfied by both the production
// pgxpool reader and the test PostgresMock.
type LegacyChunkLister interface {
	ListChunksByDocument(ctx context.Context, legacyDocumentID int64) ([]legacy.LegacyChunk, error)
	ListEmbeddingRefsByDocument(ctx context.Context, legacyDocumentID int64) ([]legacy.LegacyChunkEmbeddingRef, error)
}

// LegacyCorpusLister narrows the production PostgresReader interface to
// what reconcile actually uses.
type LegacyCorpusLister interface {
	ListCorpora(ctx context.Context, legacyOrgID int64) ([]legacy.LegacyCorpus, error)
}

// LegacyDocumentLister narrows the production PostgresReader interface
// to what reconcile actually uses.
type LegacyDocumentLister interface {
	ListDocuments(ctx context.Context, legacyOrgID int64) ([]legacy.LegacyDocument, error)
}

// Clients groups the per-phase gRPC Get stubs reconcile needs.
// Production wires the real generated clients; tests inject fakes.
// Any nil field disables deep-spot-check for that phase (count-parity
// is still emitted from the sidecar).
type Clients struct {
	EntityType       EntityTypeGetClient
	RelationshipType RelationshipTypeGetClient
	Corpus           CorpusGetClient
	Document         DocumentGetClient
	Entity           EntityGetClient
	Edge             EdgeGetClient
}

// Sidecars groups the JSON sidecar maps written by the apply phases.
// All maps are legacy_id → new UUID. Empty / nil maps are tolerated —
// reconcile reports CountParityOK=true when both legacy and sidecar
// are empty (vacuously true) and skips deep-spot-check.
type Sidecars struct {
	EntityType       map[string]string
	RelationshipType map[string]string
	Corpus           map[string]string
	Document         map[string]string
	Chunk            map[string]string
	Entity           map[string]string
	Edge             map[string]string
}

// Input gathers everything Reconcile needs. Tests construct this
// directly; the cmd/server entrypoint constructs it from cfg + readers
// + sidecars on disk.
type Input struct {
	LegacyMemgraph legacy.MemgraphReader
	LegacyCorpus   LegacyCorpusLister
	LegacyDocument LegacyDocumentLister
	LegacyChunks   LegacyChunkLister
	Clients        Clients
	Sidecars       Sidecars
	LegacyOrgID    int
	OrgID          string
	SampleSize     int
	// Rng is the random source used for sampling. Tests inject a
	// deterministic source; production passes nil and reconcile
	// constructs one from time.Now().
	Rng *rand.Rand
}

// Report is the top-level reconcile outcome. Mismatches sums sample
// mismatches across every phase plus phases that failed count parity.
type Report struct {
	RunID      string                  `json:"run_id"`
	OrgID      string                  `json:"org_id"`
	Phases     map[string]*PhaseReport `json:"phases"`
	Mismatches int                     `json:"mismatches"`
	StartedAt  time.Time               `json:"started_at"`
	FinishedAt time.Time               `json:"finished_at"`
}

// PhaseReport is the per-phase outcome.
type PhaseReport struct {
	Phase            string   `json:"phase"`
	LegacyCount      int      `json:"legacy_count"`
	NewCount         int      `json:"new_count"`
	SidecarCount     int      `json:"sidecar_count"`
	CountParityOK    bool     `json:"count_parity_ok"`
	SampleSize       int      `json:"sample_size"`
	SampleMismatches int      `json:"sample_mismatches"`
	SampleErrors     int      `json:"sample_errors"`
	Notes            []string `json:"notes,omitempty"`
}

// Reconcile runs every phase's count + deep-spot-check and returns the
// aggregate Report. Per-phase failures are captured in the PhaseReport
// rather than aborting the whole run — operators want to see the full
// surface even when one phase is broken.
func Reconcile(ctx context.Context, in Input) (*Report, error) {
	if in.LegacyOrgID <= 0 {
		return nil, errors.New("reconcile: legacy_org_id must be > 0")
	}
	if in.OrgID == "" {
		return nil, errors.New("reconcile: org_id is required")
	}
	if in.SampleSize <= 0 {
		in.SampleSize = DefaultSampleSize
	}
	if in.Rng == nil {
		// math/rand/v2: PCG seeded from monotonic + wall clock.
		now := time.Now()
		in.Rng = rand.New(rand.NewPCG(uint64(now.UnixNano()), uint64(now.Unix()))) //nolint:gosec // sampling, not crypto
	}

	startedAt := time.Now().UTC()
	report := &Report{
		RunID:     startedAt.Format("20060102T150405Z"),
		OrgID:     in.OrgID,
		Phases:    map[string]*PhaseReport{},
		StartedAt: startedAt,
	}

	type phaseRun struct {
		name string
		fn   func(context.Context, Input) *PhaseReport
	}
	runs := []phaseRun{
		{"entity-types", reconcileEntityTypes},
		{"relationship-types", reconcileRelationshipTypes},
		{"corpora", reconcileCorpora},
		{"documents", reconcileDocuments},
		{"chunks", reconcileChunks},
		{"embeddings", reconcileEmbeddings},
		{"entities", reconcileEntities},
		{"edges", reconcileEdges},
		{"provenance", reconcileProvenance},
	}

	for _, r := range runs {
		pr := r.fn(ctx, in)
		report.Phases[r.name] = pr
		if !pr.CountParityOK {
			report.Mismatches++
		}
		report.Mismatches += pr.SampleMismatches
	}

	report.FinishedAt = time.Now().UTC()
	return report, nil
}

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------
// Phase 1: entity-types
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------

func reconcileEntityTypes(ctx context.Context, in Input) *PhaseReport {
	pr := &PhaseReport{Phase: "entity-types", CountParityOK: true}

	if in.LegacyMemgraph == nil {
		pr.Notes = append(pr.Notes, "legacy memgraph reader unset; phase skipped")
		return pr
	}
	legacyRows, err := in.LegacyMemgraph.ListEntityTypes(ctx, in.LegacyOrgID)
	if err != nil {
		pr.Notes = append(pr.Notes, fmt.Sprintf("legacy list error: %v", err))
		pr.CountParityOK = false
		return pr
	}

	pr.LegacyCount = len(legacyRows)
	pr.SidecarCount = len(in.Sidecars.EntityType)
	pr.NewCount = pr.SidecarCount
	pr.CountParityOK = pr.LegacyCount == pr.NewCount

	// Deep-spot-check: dereference a random sample of legacy_ids and
	// compare names. EntityTypeService.Get returns the EntityType by
	// new-uuid; we resolve via the sidecar.
	if in.Clients.EntityType == nil {
		pr.Notes = append(pr.Notes, "entity-type Get RPC unwired; deep-spot-check skipped")
		return pr
	}

	legacyByKey := map[string]legacy.EntityType{}
	for _, r := range legacyRows {
		legacyByKey[r.LegacyID] = r
	}

	keys := pickSampleKeys(in.Sidecars.EntityType, in.SampleSize, in.Rng)
	pr.SampleSize = len(keys)
	for _, k := range keys {
		newID := in.Sidecars.EntityType[k]
		resp, err := in.Clients.EntityType.Get(ctx, &entitytypev1.GetRequest{EntityTypeId: newID})
		if err != nil {
			pr.SampleErrors++
			appendNoteCapped(pr, fmt.Sprintf("Get(%s) failed: %v", k, err))
			continue
		}
		got := resp.GetEntityType()
		want, ok := legacyByKey[k]
		if !ok {
			pr.SampleErrors++
			appendNoteCapped(pr, fmt.Sprintf("legacy row missing for sidecar key %s", k))
			continue
		}
		if got.GetName() != want.Name {
			pr.SampleMismatches++
			appendNoteCapped(pr, fmt.Sprintf("name mismatch for %s: legacy=%q new=%q", k, want.Name, got.GetName()))
		}
	}
	return pr
}

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------
// Phase 2: relationship-types
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------

func reconcileRelationshipTypes(ctx context.Context, in Input) *PhaseReport {
	pr := &PhaseReport{Phase: "relationship-types", CountParityOK: true}

	if in.LegacyMemgraph == nil {
		pr.Notes = append(pr.Notes, "legacy memgraph reader unset; phase skipped")
		return pr
	}
	legacyRows, err := in.LegacyMemgraph.ListRelationshipTypes(ctx, in.LegacyOrgID)
	if err != nil {
		pr.Notes = append(pr.Notes, fmt.Sprintf("legacy list error: %v", err))
		pr.CountParityOK = false
		return pr
	}

	pr.LegacyCount = len(legacyRows)
	pr.SidecarCount = len(in.Sidecars.RelationshipType)
	pr.NewCount = pr.SidecarCount
	pr.CountParityOK = pr.LegacyCount == pr.NewCount

	if in.Clients.RelationshipType == nil {
		pr.Notes = append(pr.Notes, "relationship-type Get RPC unwired; deep-spot-check skipped")
		return pr
	}

	legacyByKey := map[string]legacy.RelationshipType{}
	for _, r := range legacyRows {
		legacyByKey[r.LegacyID] = r
	}

	keys := pickSampleKeys(in.Sidecars.RelationshipType, in.SampleSize, in.Rng)
	pr.SampleSize = len(keys)
	for _, k := range keys {
		newID := in.Sidecars.RelationshipType[k]
		resp, err := in.Clients.RelationshipType.Get(ctx, &relationshiptypev1.GetRequest{RelationshipTypeId: newID})
		if err != nil {
			pr.SampleErrors++
			appendNoteCapped(pr, fmt.Sprintf("Get(%s) failed: %v", k, err))
			continue
		}
		got := resp.GetRelationshipType()
		want, ok := legacyByKey[k]
		if !ok {
			pr.SampleErrors++
			appendNoteCapped(pr, fmt.Sprintf("legacy row missing for sidecar key %s", k))
			continue
		}
		if got.GetName() != want.Name {
			pr.SampleMismatches++
			appendNoteCapped(pr, fmt.Sprintf("name mismatch for %s: legacy=%q new=%q", k, want.Name, got.GetName()))
		}
	}
	return pr
}

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------
// Phase 3: corpora
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------

func reconcileCorpora(ctx context.Context, in Input) *PhaseReport {
	pr := &PhaseReport{Phase: "corpora", CountParityOK: true}

	if in.LegacyCorpus == nil {
		pr.Notes = append(pr.Notes, "legacy corpus reader unset; phase skipped")
		return pr
	}
	legacyRows, err := in.LegacyCorpus.ListCorpora(ctx, int64(in.LegacyOrgID))
	if err != nil {
		pr.Notes = append(pr.Notes, fmt.Sprintf("legacy list error: %v", err))
		pr.CountParityOK = false
		return pr
	}

	pr.LegacyCount = len(legacyRows)
	pr.SidecarCount = len(in.Sidecars.Corpus)
	pr.NewCount = pr.SidecarCount
	pr.CountParityOK = pr.LegacyCount == pr.NewCount

	if in.Clients.Corpus == nil {
		pr.Notes = append(pr.Notes, "corpus Get RPC unwired; deep-spot-check skipped")
		return pr
	}

	legacyByKey := map[string]legacy.LegacyCorpus{}
	for _, r := range legacyRows {
		key := fmt.Sprintf("legacy:corpus:%d", r.LegacyID)
		legacyByKey[key] = r
	}

	keys := pickSampleKeys(in.Sidecars.Corpus, in.SampleSize, in.Rng)
	pr.SampleSize = len(keys)
	for _, k := range keys {
		newID := in.Sidecars.Corpus[k]
		resp, err := in.Clients.Corpus.Get(ctx, &corpusv1.GetRequest{CorpusId: newID})
		if err != nil {
			pr.SampleErrors++
			appendNoteCapped(pr, fmt.Sprintf("Get(%s) failed: %v", k, err))
			continue
		}
		got := resp.GetCorpus()
		want, ok := legacyByKey[k]
		if !ok {
			pr.SampleErrors++
			appendNoteCapped(pr, fmt.Sprintf("legacy row missing for sidecar key %s", k))
			continue
		}
		if got.GetName() != want.Name {
			pr.SampleMismatches++
			appendNoteCapped(pr, fmt.Sprintf("name mismatch for %s: legacy=%q new=%q", k, want.Name, got.GetName()))
		}
	}
	return pr
}

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------
// Phase 4: documents
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------

func reconcileDocuments(ctx context.Context, in Input) *PhaseReport {
	pr := &PhaseReport{Phase: "documents", CountParityOK: true}

	if in.LegacyDocument == nil {
		pr.Notes = append(pr.Notes, "legacy document reader unset; phase skipped")
		return pr
	}
	legacyRows, err := in.LegacyDocument.ListDocuments(ctx, int64(in.LegacyOrgID))
	if err != nil {
		pr.Notes = append(pr.Notes, fmt.Sprintf("legacy list error: %v", err))
		pr.CountParityOK = false
		return pr
	}

	pr.LegacyCount = len(legacyRows)
	pr.SidecarCount = len(in.Sidecars.Document)
	pr.NewCount = pr.SidecarCount
	pr.CountParityOK = pr.LegacyCount == pr.NewCount

	if in.Clients.Document == nil {
		pr.Notes = append(pr.Notes, "document Get RPC unwired; deep-spot-check skipped")
		return pr
	}

	legacyByKey := map[string]legacy.LegacyDocument{}
	for _, r := range legacyRows {
		key := fmt.Sprintf("legacy:document:%d", r.LegacyID)
		legacyByKey[key] = r
	}

	keys := pickSampleKeys(in.Sidecars.Document, in.SampleSize, in.Rng)
	pr.SampleSize = len(keys)
	for _, k := range keys {
		newID := in.Sidecars.Document[k]
		resp, err := in.Clients.Document.Get(ctx, &documentv1.GetRequest{DocumentId: newID})
		if err != nil {
			pr.SampleErrors++
			appendNoteCapped(pr, fmt.Sprintf("Get(%s) failed: %v", k, err))
			continue
		}
		got := resp.GetDocument()
		want, ok := legacyByKey[k]
		if !ok {
			pr.SampleErrors++
			appendNoteCapped(pr, fmt.Sprintf("legacy row missing for sidecar key %s", k))
			continue
		}
		// Filename + size are stable; mime type is mapper-derived
		// (legacy "pdf" → "application/pdf") so we don't compare it
		// here — that's mapper coverage territory.
		if got.GetFilename() != want.OriginalFilename {
			pr.SampleMismatches++
			appendNoteCapped(pr, fmt.Sprintf("filename mismatch for %s: legacy=%q new=%q", k, want.OriginalFilename, got.GetFilename()))
			continue
		}
		if got.GetSizeBytes() != want.SizeBytes {
			pr.SampleMismatches++
			appendNoteCapped(pr, fmt.Sprintf("size_bytes mismatch for %s: legacy=%d new=%d", k, want.SizeBytes, got.GetSizeBytes()))
		}
	}
	return pr
}

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------
// Phase 5: chunks
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------

func reconcileChunks(ctx context.Context, in Input) *PhaseReport {
	pr := &PhaseReport{Phase: "chunks", CountParityOK: true}

	if in.LegacyChunks == nil {
		pr.Notes = append(pr.Notes, "legacy chunk reader unset; phase skipped")
		return pr
	}

	// Sum chunks across every legacy document referenced by the
	// document_map. We deliberately drive iteration off the sidecar
	// rather than re-listing documents — the document_map is the
	// definition of which documents Phase 4 successfully migrated.
	legacyTotal := 0
	for legacyDocKey := range in.Sidecars.Document {
		// Sidecar keys are "legacy:document:<int>" — extract the int.
		var docID int64
		if _, err := fmt.Sscanf(legacyDocKey, "legacy:document:%d", &docID); err != nil {
			continue
		}
		rows, err := in.LegacyChunks.ListChunksByDocument(ctx, docID)
		if err != nil {
			pr.Notes = append(pr.Notes, fmt.Sprintf("legacy chunk list doc=%d error: %v", docID, err))
			pr.CountParityOK = false
			return pr
		}
		legacyTotal += len(rows)
	}

	pr.LegacyCount = legacyTotal
	pr.SidecarCount = len(in.Sidecars.Chunk)
	pr.NewCount = pr.SidecarCount
	pr.CountParityOK = pr.LegacyCount == pr.NewCount

	// Deep-spot-check is structurally awkward for chunks: the new
	// platform doesn't expose a per-chunk Get RPC (chunks are listed
	// per-document via DocumentService.List variant we don't wire
	// in this task). Skip and document the gap.
	pr.Notes = append(pr.Notes, "deep-spot-check skipped: files-svc has no per-chunk Get RPC; relying on count parity via sidecar")
	return pr
}

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------
// Phase 6: embeddings
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------

func reconcileEmbeddings(ctx context.Context, in Input) *PhaseReport {
	pr := &PhaseReport{Phase: "embeddings", CountParityOK: true}

	if in.LegacyChunks == nil {
		pr.Notes = append(pr.Notes, "legacy chunk reader unset; phase skipped")
		return pr
	}

	// Sum legacy embedding refs across every document Phase 4
	// migrated. The new-platform side doesn't expose a per-embedding
	// Get RPC (embeddings are stored as a Qdrant point keyed by the
	// chunk's embedding_id, not addressable from files-svc), so
	// we cannot count the new side from the migrator. We treat the
	// chunk_map count as a ceiling — every successfully-migrated
	// chunk should have an embedding when the legacy side did, and
	// the apply phase tracks that via PointsFetched/EmbeddingsWritten
	// in its own report.
	legacyTotal := 0
	for legacyDocKey := range in.Sidecars.Document {
		var docID int64
		if _, err := fmt.Sscanf(legacyDocKey, "legacy:document:%d", &docID); err != nil {
			continue
		}
		refs, err := in.LegacyChunks.ListEmbeddingRefsByDocument(ctx, docID)
		if err != nil {
			pr.Notes = append(pr.Notes, fmt.Sprintf("legacy embedding-ref list doc=%d error: %v", docID, err))
			pr.CountParityOK = false
			return pr
		}
		legacyTotal += len(refs)
	}

	pr.LegacyCount = legacyTotal
	// No sidecar for embeddings (apply phase doesn't write one — the
	// chunk_map.json is the indirect ledger). NewCount stays 0 from
	// the migrator's perspective; the operator must consult Phase 6's
	// apply RESULT JSON for EmbeddingsWritten to confirm parity.
	pr.SidecarCount = 0
	pr.NewCount = 0
	if legacyTotal == 0 {
		// Vacuously parity-true when both sides are empty.
		pr.CountParityOK = true
	} else {
		// Cannot reconcile from the migrator side — see note.
		pr.CountParityOK = false
	}
	pr.Notes = append(pr.Notes,
		"embeddings have no sidecar; reconcile cannot compare counts from the migrator side",
		"check Phase 6 apply RESULT.embeddings_written vs legacy_count above for go/no-go",
	)
	return pr
}

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------
// Phase 7: entities
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------

func reconcileEntities(ctx context.Context, in Input) *PhaseReport {
	pr := &PhaseReport{Phase: "entities", CountParityOK: true}

	if in.LegacyMemgraph == nil {
		pr.Notes = append(pr.Notes, "legacy memgraph reader unset; phase skipped")
		return pr
	}
	legacyRows, err := in.LegacyMemgraph.ListEntities(ctx, in.LegacyOrgID)
	if err != nil {
		pr.Notes = append(pr.Notes, fmt.Sprintf("legacy list error: %v", err))
		pr.CountParityOK = false
		return pr
	}

	pr.LegacyCount = len(legacyRows)
	pr.SidecarCount = len(in.Sidecars.Entity)
	pr.NewCount = pr.SidecarCount
	pr.CountParityOK = pr.LegacyCount == pr.NewCount

	if in.Clients.Entity == nil {
		pr.Notes = append(pr.Notes, "entity Get RPC unwired; deep-spot-check skipped")
		return pr
	}

	legacyByKey := map[string]legacy.LegacyEntity{}
	for _, r := range legacyRows {
		legacyByKey[r.LegacyID] = r
	}

	keys := pickSampleKeys(in.Sidecars.Entity, in.SampleSize, in.Rng)
	pr.SampleSize = len(keys)
	for _, k := range keys {
		newID := in.Sidecars.Entity[k]
		resp, err := in.Clients.Entity.Get(ctx, &entityv1.GetRequest{EntityId: newID})
		if err != nil {
			pr.SampleErrors++
			appendNoteCapped(pr, fmt.Sprintf("Get(%s) failed: %v", k, err))
			continue
		}
		got := resp.GetEntity()
		want, ok := legacyByKey[k]
		if !ok {
			pr.SampleErrors++
			appendNoteCapped(pr, fmt.Sprintf("legacy row missing for sidecar key %s", k))
			continue
		}
		if got.GetLabel() != want.Label {
			pr.SampleMismatches++
			appendNoteCapped(pr, fmt.Sprintf("label mismatch for %s: legacy=%q new=%q", k, want.Label, got.GetLabel()))
		}
	}
	return pr
}

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------
// Phase 8: edges
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------

func reconcileEdges(ctx context.Context, in Input) *PhaseReport {
	pr := &PhaseReport{Phase: "edges", CountParityOK: true}

	if in.LegacyMemgraph == nil {
		pr.Notes = append(pr.Notes, "legacy memgraph reader unset; phase skipped")
		return pr
	}
	legacyRows, err := in.LegacyMemgraph.ListEdges(ctx, in.LegacyOrgID)
	if err != nil {
		pr.Notes = append(pr.Notes, fmt.Sprintf("legacy list error: %v", err))
		pr.CountParityOK = false
		return pr
	}

	pr.LegacyCount = len(legacyRows)
	pr.SidecarCount = len(in.Sidecars.Edge)
	pr.NewCount = pr.SidecarCount
	pr.CountParityOK = pr.LegacyCount == pr.NewCount

	if in.Clients.Edge == nil {
		pr.Notes = append(pr.Notes, "edge Get RPC unwired; deep-spot-check skipped")
		return pr
	}

	legacyByKey := map[string]legacy.LegacyEdge{}
	for _, r := range legacyRows {
		legacyByKey[r.LegacyID] = r
	}

	// Endpoint resolution: when comparing a sampled edge, we need
	// the new source/target UUIDs as the new edge stores. The
	// entity_map sidecar maps "legacy:entity:<id>" → new UUID; we
	// expect the new edge's source_id/target_id to match.
	keys := pickSampleKeys(in.Sidecars.Edge, in.SampleSize, in.Rng)
	pr.SampleSize = len(keys)
	for _, k := range keys {
		newID := in.Sidecars.Edge[k]
		resp, err := in.Clients.Edge.Get(ctx, &edgev1.GetRequest{EdgeId: newID})
		if err != nil {
			pr.SampleErrors++
			appendNoteCapped(pr, fmt.Sprintf("Get(%s) failed: %v", k, err))
			continue
		}
		got := resp.GetEdge()
		want, ok := legacyByKey[k]
		if !ok {
			pr.SampleErrors++
			appendNoteCapped(pr, fmt.Sprintf("legacy row missing for sidecar key %s", k))
			continue
		}
		// Compare resolved source/target UUIDs — the edge migrated
		// successfully iff its endpoints in the new platform match
		// the entity_map's translation of the legacy endpoints.
		expectSrc := in.Sidecars.Entity[want.SourceLegacyID]
		expectTgt := in.Sidecars.Entity[want.TargetLegacyID]
		if expectSrc != "" && got.GetSourceId() != expectSrc {
			pr.SampleMismatches++
			appendNoteCapped(pr, fmt.Sprintf("source_id mismatch for %s: expected=%s new=%s", k, expectSrc, got.GetSourceId()))
			continue
		}
		if expectTgt != "" && got.GetTargetId() != expectTgt {
			pr.SampleMismatches++
			appendNoteCapped(pr, fmt.Sprintf("target_id mismatch for %s: expected=%s new=%s", k, expectTgt, got.GetTargetId()))
		}
	}
	return pr
}

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------
// Phase 9: provenance
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------

func reconcileProvenance(ctx context.Context, in Input) *PhaseReport {
	pr := &PhaseReport{Phase: "provenance", CountParityOK: true}

	if in.LegacyMemgraph == nil {
		pr.Notes = append(pr.Notes, "legacy memgraph reader unset; phase skipped")
		return pr
	}

	entLinks, err := in.LegacyMemgraph.ListEntityProvenance(ctx, in.LegacyOrgID)
	if err != nil {
		pr.Notes = append(pr.Notes, fmt.Sprintf("legacy entity provenance list error: %v", err))
		pr.CountParityOK = false
		return pr
	}
	edgeLinks, err := in.LegacyMemgraph.ListEdgeProvenance(ctx, in.LegacyOrgID)
	if err != nil {
		pr.Notes = append(pr.Notes, fmt.Sprintf("legacy edge provenance list error: %v", err))
		pr.CountParityOK = false
		return pr
	}

	pr.LegacyCount = len(entLinks) + len(edgeLinks)
	// No sidecar — provenance is terminal (Phase 9 doesn't emit one).
	pr.SidecarCount = 0
	pr.NewCount = 0
	pr.CountParityOK = pr.LegacyCount == 0
	pr.Notes = append(pr.Notes,
		"legacy stores entity↔Document provenance only (no chunk granularity)",
		"Phase 9 readers return empty by design — see legacy.ProvenanceLink godoc",
		"reconcile reports 0 vs 0 as parity-OK",
	)
	return pr
}

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------
// Helpers
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------

// pickSampleKeys returns up to `size` keys from the sidecar map,
// chosen uniformly at random. Order is deterministic given the same
// rng — keys are sorted before sampling so test seeds are stable
// across Go versions / map iteration orders.
//
// When size >= len(sidecar), all keys are returned (in sorted order
// for determinism).
func pickSampleKeys(sidecar map[string]string, size int, rng *rand.Rand) []string {
	if len(sidecar) == 0 || size <= 0 {
		return nil
	}
	keys := make([]string, 0, len(sidecar))
	for k := range sidecar {
		keys = append(keys, k)
	}
	sort.Strings(keys)
	if size >= len(keys) {
		return keys
	}
	// Fisher-Yates partial shuffle: O(size) instead of O(n) for
	// small samples on large maps.
	for i := 0; i < size; i++ {
		j := i + rng.IntN(len(keys)-i)
		keys[i], keys[j] = keys[j], keys[i]
	}
	return keys[:size]
}

// appendNoteCapped adds a note to PhaseReport.Notes only while the
// list is below maxNotePerSampledMismatch — keeps reconcile.json
// bounded even when every row mismatches.
func appendNoteCapped(pr *PhaseReport, note string) {
	if len(pr.Notes) >= maxNotePerSampledMismatch {
		return
	}
	pr.Notes = append(pr.Notes, note)
}

// Compile-time guard: production target.Files fields satisfy our
// narrowed Get-only interfaces. Keeps the cmd/server wiring honest —
// if the generated client signatures change, reconcile fails to
// build, not at runtime.
var (
	_ EntityTypeGetClient       = (entitytypev1.EntityTypeServiceClient)(nil)
	_ RelationshipTypeGetClient = (relationshiptypev1.RelationshipTypeServiceClient)(nil)
	_ CorpusGetClient           = (corpusv1.CorpusServiceClient)(nil)
	_ DocumentGetClient         = (documentv1.DocumentServiceClient)(nil)
	_ EntityGetClient           = (entityv1.EntityServiceClient)(nil)
	_ EdgeGetClient             = (edgev1.EdgeServiceClient)(nil)
)



